{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall take two, etc.</b> One needs to know why it says <b>et</b>, etc. And perhaps it intends the shoham stones, which He had already mentioned at the beginning of the command in parashat Terumah (Exodus 25:7). And this is the gist of the verse: ״וְלָקַחְתָּ אֶת שְׁתֵּי אַבְנֵי שֹׁהַם אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ לְהָבִיא״. And in this, the sweetness of His words, may He be blessed, is intended — to give a reason why He singled out the shoham stones from among all the stones, for the shoham stones have one specific commandment apart from the stones of the breastplate; therefore He said to him <b>and you shall take them, shoham stones</b> — which I have specified for you."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:08.615953581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}